From 9f9115668241a11c4867f86ae6892358f6c5846c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlobProps <blobprops@local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:26:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 0135] gpu31-kms: blob properties and CRTC MODE_ID (int84)

kwin_wayland 6.8 drops the only CRTC because DrmCrtc::updateProperties()
requires MODE_ID and ACTIVE on the CRTC object; the v4.0 atomic backport
(M0 0001-0005) has no MODE_ID and no CREATE/DESTROYPROPBLOB ioctls.

Backport the v4.2 blob property core:
  - struct drm_property_blob gains dev, kref refcount, head_global,
    head_file and a size_t length (was a bare list_head); blobs are now
    refcounted and tracked per file handle (drm_file::blobs).
  - drm_property_create_blob()/lookup_blob()/reference_blob()/
    unreference_blob()/destroy_user_blobs() plus a private
    __drm_property_lookup_blob(); the 3.10 static create/destroy pair in
    drm_crtc.c is replaced.
  - mode_config.blob_lock protects the global and per-file lists and is
    held around idr insert/remove; drm_mode_config_cleanup() drops the
    remaining blobs instead of freeing them directly.
  - drm_mode_getblob_ioctl() looks the blob up under blob_lock (was a
    lock-free drm_mode_object_find); drm_mode_getproperty_ioctl() keeps
    reporting count_enum_blobs = 0 for blob properties (the 3.10 branch
    walked a list no blob was ever added to).
  - DRM_IOCTL_MODE_CREATEPROPBLOB (0xBD) / DESTROYPROPBLOB (0xBE) with
    struct drm_mode_create_blob/drm_mode_destroy_blob, wired in
    drm_drv.c next to GETPROPBLOB.
  - drm_release() destroys a client's blobs with the file.

CRTC MODE_ID:
  - "MODE_ID" (ATOMIC|BLOB) is created in
    drm_mode_create_standard_properties() and attached to every CRTC by
    drm_crtc_init_with_planes() when DRIVER_ATOMIC is set.
  - drm_crtc_state.mode_blob holds the state's reference; the helper
    reset/duplicate/destroy hooks take and drop it.
  - drm_atomic_set_mode_prop_for_crtc() validates the blob length and
    converts it with drm_mode_convert_umode() into state->mode, so a
    MODE_ID commit programs that mode; drm_atomic_set_mode_for_crtc() is
    the kernel-side counterpart and drm_atomic_helper_set_config() uses
    it instead of poking state->mode/enable directly.
  - drm_atomic_crtc_set_property()/get_property() handle prop_mode_id and
    prop_active; the set path used to return -EINVAL even after storing
    ACTIVE, which would have failed every KWin commit.
  - drm_crtc_convert_umode()/drm_crtc_convert_to_umode() become the
    public v4.2 drm_mode_convert_umode()/drm_mode_convert_to_umode();
    umode now also rejects a mode that fails drm_mode_validate_basic().

Expected userspace change: modetest -c lists MODE_ID on the CRTC and
KWin's DrmCrtc initialises; its atomic commit carries the mode blob.

Series: drm-atomic/0001-0005 -> drm-kms 0104..0130/0133 -> 0134 -> this.
Compile: make ARCH=arm64 CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-gnu-
KCFLAGS=-Wno-error -j8 drivers/gpu/drm/ rc=0 (KMS config,
CONFIG_DRM_EXYNOS7580=y). Report: docs/reports/drm-blob-props-backport.md
